<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S&amp;J Land attrib loss shrinks, no div.</title>
<headline>S&amp;J Land attrib loss shrinks, no div.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended December 31, 1996</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr, attrib loss (cts)</p>
<p>				  0.3	   vs 2.3</p>
<p>    Attrib loss	     0.09	  vs 0.60</p>
<p>    Tax			 nil	   vs nil</p>
<p>    Net interest received 0.62	  vs 0.57</p>
<p>    Operating loss	  0.70	  vs 0.23</p>
<p>    Abnormal item	   nil	   vs 0.95</p>
<p>    Turnover		  0.55	  vs 6.18</p>
<p>Full name: S &amp; J Land Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Diretors said the fall in turnover was attributable to reduced property sales. They said the removal of mine dumps in some sectors of the company's property was progressing. Negotiations for the resettlement of illegal occupants on parts of the firm's land was being negotiated.</p>
<p>They said negotiations were taking place with regard to the proposed sale of an additional 7.5 hectares of property.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
